1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,604
Start in Content library, then Sales kits. The first kit brings together ANC venue technology,

2
00:00:06,604 --> 00:00:11,608
creative, project examples, and a talk track for a first client conversation.

3
00:00:12,408 --> 00:00:18,563
Enter the client, venue, meeting goal, and presenter. The presentation preview updates with those details.

4
00:00:18,563 --> 00:00:22,256
Here we are preparing an ANC Studios venue showcase.

5
00:00:23,056 --> 00:00:27,368
Click a section to preview it. Keep the sections that fit the conversation.

6
00:00:27,368 --> 00:00:31,348
The opening and closing stay included, with at least one additional section.

7
00:00:31,348 --> 00:00:34,001
Open the talk track for a speaking cue.

8
00:00:34,801 --> 00:00:39,333
Matching venue creative is included below. Preview the ANC Studios reel,

9
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:43,866
or download the reel and transparent ANC logo for venue screens.

10
00:00:43,866 --> 00:00:47,574
The project examples remain clearly identified as reference venues.

11
00:00:48,374 --> 00:00:52,744
Choose Create client presentation. You now have a saved, editable copy.

12
00:00:52,744 --> 00:00:59,100
Open the presentation to review its sections and make the final adjustments before sharing it with

13
00:00:59,100 --> 00:00:59,894
the client.

14
00:01:00,694 --> 00:01:05,612
Open the sales brief for the meeting goal and section-by-section talking points.

15
00:01:05,612 --> 00:01:12,169
These notes stay inside the workspace. They are excluded from the client presentation link and presentation

16
00:01:12,169 --> 00:01:12,579
PDF.

17
00:01:13,379 --> 00:01:18,556
For the creative team, Review kit source shows the master sections and their talk tracks.

18
00:01:18,556 --> 00:01:24,078
Edit the master in the builder, reload the source, and review the material before publishing a

19
00:01:24,078 --> 00:01:24,768
kit revision.

20
00:01:25,568 --> 00:01:31,346
A published kit revision supplies future presentations. Existing client copies stay unchanged.

21
00:01:31,346 --> 00:01:39,050
Designers maintain the standard; sales personalizes the conversation; Natalia can assemble the prepared material and review

22
00:01:39,050 --> 00:01:40,013
the result.
